## Context

IT seems that a method call in Placebo is expecting that the [eventbus](https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire/Placebo/blob/66ad24d17476a5f8cb2822a014132c3759011499/src/main/java/dev/shadowsoffire/placebo/Placebo.java#L52) is an `EventBus` instance to call `start()`. However, SpongeNeo replaces this eventbus with its own to keep symmetrical compatibility between SpongeAPI implementation of it's [EventManager](https://github.com/SpongePowered/Sponge/blob/60a813bfe0987d2c71113f3d39eda79b719b4904/src/main/java/org/spongepowered/common/event/manager/SpongeEventManager.java#L78) and Neo [events and their listeners](https://github.com/SpongePowered/Sponge/blob/60a813bfe0987d2c71113f3d39eda79b719b4904/neoforge/src/launch/java/org/spongepowered/neoforge/launch/event/NeoEventManager.java#L43). It seems that the method `start()` is available on the `IEventBus` interface, so would it be suitable to simply call that instead, since SpongeNeo can easily forward that to the wrapped instance?

Placebo: 9.2.2
